{"name":"Cocktail Hour","hex":"#fd9a52","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cocktail","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixed alcoholic beverage.","A mixture of other substances or things."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Ostentatiously lacking in manners."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cocktail"},{"term":"hour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A unit of time of one twenty-fourth of a day (sixty minutes).","A season, moment, or time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Happy hour","blocks":[{"text":"Happy hour is a marketing term for a time of day when a venue such as a restaurant or bar offers reduced prices on alcoholic drinks. Menu items like appetizers are also often offered at a discounted price during happy hour. This is a way for bars and restaurants to draw in more business before or after peak business hours."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Happy_hour","wikidata":"Q1364401"},{"title":"Cocktail Hour (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cocktail Hour is a 1933 American pre-Code romantic drama film produced and distributed by Columbia Pictures and starring Bebe Daniels. This film was directed by Victor Schertzinger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Cocktail_Hour_lobby_card.jpg/330px-Cocktail_Hour_lobby_card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocktail_Hour_(film)","wikidata":"Q16249410"},{"title":"Cocktail","blocks":[{"text":"A cocktail is a mixed drink, usually alcoholic. Most commonly, a cocktail is a combination of one or more spirits mixed with other ingredients, such as juices, flavored syrups, tonic water, shrubs, and bitters. Cocktails vary widely across regions of the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/15-09-26-RalfR-WLC-0084.jpg/330px-15-09-26-RalfR-WLC-0084.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.or